      "side": 1,
      "message": "Something like?\n\nCONFIG_MKBP_USE_HOST_EVENT:\nSend MKBP event over the only communication method available: inband eSPI/LPC notification which eventually triggers an SCI event. This is to be done only when there\u0027s no GPIO available on older boards. Warning: A high jitter to be expected by using this method.\n\n\nCONFIG_MKBP_USE_GPIO:\nSend MKBP event over a GPIO. Usually used in systems where the EC-AP protocol is simple (SPI or I2C). The GPIO doubles as a wake from S3.\n\n(last sentence pending our other conversation)",
